drydock-hail-service = Drydock services

drydock-hail-greeting-1 = { $location }, { $name } speaking. Go ahead, { $ship }.
drydock-hail-greeting-2 = This is { $name } at { $location }. Reading you, { $ship }.
drydock-hail-greeting-3 = { $location } dockmaster. What do you need, { $ship }?

drydock-hail-offer = Open drydock services and tell me what she needs. I'll find you a berth.
drydock-hail-booked = Berth { $berth } is booked for you. Hold her still there and the work starts.
drydock-hail-working = Berth { $berth } is working on your ship, about { $minutes } min left.

drydock-dockmaster-greeting = Dockmaster's desk. What can the drydock do for you?
drydock-dockmaster-farewell = Mind the cranes.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-how = How does the drydock work?
drydock-dockmaster-response-how = Hail me, or use the services console at my desk, to see what the drydock can do for your ship and book it. I assign a berth that fits her. Follow the green lights into the frame and hold still. Payment is taken when the cranes start. Leave mid-job and unfinished work is refunded. Cranes skip parts they can't reach and refund those too.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-hail = Do I have to come in person?
drydock-dockmaster-response-hail = Not at all. Hail me from your helm's HAIL page, windowed or in the cockpit, and pick drydock services. I'll book the smallest berth that fits your ship.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-who = Who are you?
drydock-dockmaster-response-who = Ilse Brannock, dockmaster. I keep both bays turning and the cranes off people's heads.
